It is a mighty beanstalk which descends to the ground far below.	這是一株雄偉的豆莖，一路延伸到遙遠下方的地面。
You are much too high to see anything below you in any detail.	你的位置太高了，看不清楚下方的任何細節。
You're too busy	你正忙著呢
All you can hear is the quiet drip of water from the roof of the cave.	你只聽得見洞頂滴落的水滴聲，靜悄悄的。
This cave smells musty and damp.	這個洞穴聞起來又霉又潮濕。
You catch a few falling drops of water in your hand, barely enough to moisten your lips.	你用手接住幾滴落下的水，勉強夠潤濕嘴唇。
You don't have that! But there is enough light in this cave for you to see clearly.	你身上沒有那個！不過這個洞穴裡的光線足夠讓你看清楚。
The walls of this cave are damp and moldy.	這個洞穴的牆壁又濕又發霉。
The walls of this shadowy cave are too damp and steep for you to climb.	這個陰暗洞穴的牆壁又濕又陡，你爬不上去。
Apparently you're getting a little lightheaded.	看來你有點頭暈了。
You're not that hungry.	你沒那麼餓。
You're not going to need that, Sir Graham.	格拉漢爵士，你用不到那個。
When you look closely, you can see that the mold on the cave walls is glowing faintly.	你仔細一看，發現洞壁上的霉斑微微發著光。
These are of no use to you, Sir Graham.	格拉漢爵士，這些對你沒有用。
These rock formations were slowly created over thousands of years.	這些岩石地形是經過數千年慢慢形成的。
Brackish water drips slowly from the stalactites on the ceiling.	帶著鹹味的水緩緩從天花板的鐘乳石滴落。
You can see the vague, shadowy outline of a tunnel leading to the south.	你可以看見一條模糊陰暗的隧道輪廓，通往南方。
You can see the hole that you fell through in the roof of the cave, far above you.	你可以看見自己摔落的那個洞口，就在頭頂遙遠的洞頂上。
The rocky floor of the cave is covered with rotting leaves and mold.	洞穴的石質地面覆滿了腐爛的落葉與霉斑。
You are standing in a shadowy cavern. This cave is murky and damp, and smells of mold and rotted leaves.	你站在一個陰暗的洞穴裡。這個洞穴昏暗潮濕，散發著霉味與腐葉的氣味。
There is a single torch on the wall, illuminating this shadowy cave.	牆上有一支火把，照亮了這個陰暗的洞穴。
The farther you get from the light, the mustier it becomes.	你離光源越遠，霉味就越重。
The torch is too hot to touch.	火把太燙了，摸不得。
The rat grins crookedly, his long, pointed fangs glistening in the torchlight. His sense of smell alerts him of your presence.	大老鼠咧嘴歪笑，長而尖的獠牙在火光下閃著光。牠靈敏的嗅覺察覺到你的存在。
The rat grins crookedly, his long, pointed fangs glistening in the torchlight.	大老鼠咧嘴歪笑，長而尖的獠牙在火光下閃著光。
RAT: "That's right, mister, just walk a little closer...."	大老鼠：「沒錯，老兄，再靠近一點……」
Whatever makes you think there's a rat in here?	你怎麼會覺得這裡有隻老鼠？
What would you like to give the rat?	你想給大老鼠什麼？
Mouse?	老鼠？
RAT: "Hey, pal, this is no mouse you're talking to here!"	大老鼠：「嘿，老兄，你面前這位可不是什麼老鼠！」
You see a giant rat with matted fur and dripping teeth.	你看見一隻巨大老鼠，毛髮糾結，牙齒滴著口水。
Unfortunately, his teeth are larger than yours.	可惜牠的牙齒比你的大多了。
RAT: "Hey, friend.  You wanna go through this door, make me an offer, and I promise I'll letcha breeze right through."	大老鼠：「嘿，朋友。你想通過這扇門的話，給我點好處，我保證讓你輕鬆過關。」
RAT: "You're not fooling me with that ol' ring of invisibility trick!  I've seen that one a million times...er, I mean, I HAVEN'T seen that one a million times!  I can smell you there!	大老鼠：「你那套隱形戒指的把戲騙不了我！這招我看過上百萬次了……呃，我是說，我才沒看過上百萬次咧！我聞得到你在那裡！
RAT: "Hello there, my friend.  You looking for anything in particular?"	大老鼠：「你好啊，朋友。你在找什麼特別的東西嗎？」
RAT: "You wanna pass through my little door here, right?  Well, maybe we can work somethin' out.  What's it worth to you?"	大老鼠：「你想通過我這扇小門，對吧？嗯，或許我們可以談談。你願意出多少代價？」
Keeping in mind the rat's remarkable agility and even more remarkable fangs, you decide not to risk an attack.	想到大老鼠驚人的敏捷身手，還有更驚人的獠牙，你決定不冒險攻擊。
RAT: "I know you're gonna want what's behind this door. But what's in it for me?"	大老鼠：「我知道你想要這扇門後面的東西。但我能得到什麼好處？」
Since you and all you carry are invisible, the rat can't possibly see what you're trying to show him.	既然你和你身上帶的東西都隱形了，大老鼠根本不可能看見你想給牠看的東西。
The giant rat's lips quiver in anticipation at the odor of the cheese. Watch it, though, you don't want to tease this rat.	巨鼠聞到乳酪的氣味，嘴唇興奮地顫抖著。不過小心點，你可不會想招惹這隻老鼠。
The rat is a dangerous character, teasing him with that might get you into trouble.	這隻老鼠是個危險角色，拿那個逗牠可能會給你惹上麻煩。
You throw your last pebble at the rat, but in this dim light, you can't see well enough to hit your target.	你朝大老鼠丟出最後一顆鵝卵石，但光線昏暗，你看不清楚，無法擊中目標。
You throw a pebble at the rat, but in this dim light, you can't see well enough to hit your target.	你朝大老鼠丟出一顆鵝卵石，但光線昏暗，你看不清楚，無法擊中目標。
What's left to throw the pebble at?	還有什麼東西可以丟鵝卵石？
You don't have anything like that in your inventory.	你的物品欄裡沒有那樣東西。
You don't have a bucket of water.	你身上沒有一桶水。
You aren't close enough yet.	你還不夠靠近。
The rat grins, showing long, pointed teeth. "That's right, mister, just walk a little closer...."	大老鼠咧嘴一笑，露出長而尖的牙齒。「沒錯，老兄，再靠近一點……」
In the dim light, your aim would suffer.  Better to find a less violent way to get past this dirty rat.	在這昏暗的光線下，你的準頭會大打折扣。最好找個不那麼暴力的方法通過這隻髒老鼠。
There's no reason to do that, Sir Graham.	格拉漢爵士，沒有理由這麼做。
RAT: "Come a little closer.  I can't reach it!"	大老鼠：「再靠近一點。我搆不到！」
You have nothing the rat wants.	你身上沒有大老鼠想要的東西。
Whaddaya tryin' to do, cheat me with that measly offering?  What an insult.	你這是想幹嘛，用這種寒酸的東西來騙我？真是侮辱人。
I'm not sure who or what you want to bite.	我不確定你想咬的是誰、或是什麼東西。
Who do you want to talk to?	你想跟誰說話？
Who do you want to throw at?	你想朝誰丟東西？
Who?	誰？
When you attempt to count your fingers, you're horrified to see that your whole hand is missing!  Then you sheepishly remember your invisibility.	你試著數自己的手指，卻驚恐地發現整隻手都不見了！接著你才不好意思地想起，自己正處於隱形狀態。
Amazingly enough, you still have all your fingers!	說也神奇，你的手指一根不少！
You nervously count your fingers and find, to your relief, that your hand is unharmed.	你緊張地數著手指，鬆了一口氣，發現自己的手完好無損。
All you can hear is the quiet drip of water from the roof of the cave and the giant rat slavering and licking his lips.	你只聽得見洞頂滴水的靜謐聲響，還有巨鼠流著口水舔嘴唇的聲音。
This cave smells of mold and giant rat.	這個洞穴聞起來又是霉味又是巨鼠的氣味。
Are you sure you want to do that right now?  This water looks and smells awful!	你確定現在要這麼做嗎？這水看起來、聞起來都糟糕透了！
The walls of this shadowy cave are too steep for you to climb.	這個陰暗洞穴的牆壁太陡了，你爬不上去。
You're kidding, right?	你在開玩笑吧？
Do you really think you're going to need that on your quest, Sir Graham?	格拉漢爵士，你真的覺得這趟冒險會用到那個嗎？
The floor of this cave is damp with mold.	這個洞穴的地面又濕又長滿了霉斑。
You are standing in a cavern, with a wooden door directly across from you. A giant mouse is standing in front of the door.	你站在一個洞穴裡，正前方是一扇木門。一隻巨大的老鼠站在門前。
RAT: "Hey, I ain't no mouse, capishe?"	大老鼠：「嘿，我才不是什麼老鼠，懂沒？」
You are standing in a cavern, with a wooden door directly across from you.	你站在一個洞穴裡，正前方是一扇木門。
To whom do you wish to give it?	你想把它給誰？
It looks like a sturdy old door.	這看起來是一扇堅固的老舊木門。
Just walk over to it.	只要走過去就行了。
You'll need to be much closer to do that, Sir Graham.	格拉漢爵士，你得靠得更近才能這麼做。
This is a big, hungry-looking rat with slavering jaws and long, sharp claws.	這是一隻體型巨大、看起來飢餓的老鼠，下顎流著口水，還有又長又尖的爪子。
The rat's gigantic fangs look incredibly sharp, as if they could rip through unprotected flesh like a hot knife through butter.  His mouth waters and his lips quiver in anticipation of the meal he may make of you.	大老鼠碩大的獠牙看起來鋒利無比，彷彿能像熱刀切奶油一樣，輕易撕裂沒有防護的血肉。牠垂涎三尺，嘴唇興奮地顫抖著，期待著把你當成一頓大餐。
The rat's sharp, pointed claws look as deadly as his teeth!	大老鼠尖銳的爪子，看起來和牠的牙齒一樣致命！
The rat is now dripping wet.  Although he doesn't seem to mind the dampness, you haven't gotten any closer to your goal.	大老鼠現在渾身濕透。雖然牠似乎不介意這股潮濕，但你距離目標並沒有更接近。
RAT: "Cheese?  Well, yeah, now that you mention it, I guess I am kinda hungry...."	大老鼠：「乳酪？嗯，這麼一說，我好像是有點餓了……」
RAT: "Some sort of treasure?  Now you're talkin', mister.  Lemme see some of that treasure."	大老鼠：「什麼寶物？這才像話嘛，老兄。讓我瞧瞧那些寶物。」
Using his sense of smell as a guide, the rat quickly snatches it from your hand.  You might want to count your fingers.	大老鼠靠著嗅覺，迅速從你手中把東西搶走。你也許該數數自己的手指還在不在。
The rat uses his strong sense of smell as a guide and takes the treasure from your hand.	大老鼠靠著靈敏的嗅覺，從你手中拿走了那件寶物。
The rat drools at the sight of the cheese, and snatches it from your hand.  You might want to count your fingers.	大老鼠一看到乳酪就流口水，一把從你手中搶走。你也許該數數自己的手指還在不在。
The rat takes the treasure from your hand.	大老鼠從你手中拿走了那件寶物。
Using his sense of smell to guide him, the rat attacks you. In the scuffle, your ring falls off, making you visible again.	大老鼠靠著嗅覺攻擊你。一陣拉扯之間，你的戒指脫落，你再次現形。
The leprechauns' magical powers detect your unseen presence.	地穴人的魔法察覺到你隱形的存在。
This is one tight squeeze the mushroom will not get you out of.	這回的窘境，蘑菇可救不了你。
There are no leprechauns here.	這裡沒有地穴人。
They are tiny people dressed all in green.	他們是一群身形嬌小、渾身穿著綠衣的人。
This door separates the rat's warren from the domain of the Leprechaun King.	這扇門將大老鼠的巢穴與地穴人國王的領地隔開。
You are in the antechamber of the Hall of the Leprechaun King.	你站在地穴人國王大殿的前廳。
There are leprechauns in the room with you.	房間裡還有其他地穴人陪著你。
Leave the door open.  Perhaps a draft will clear out some of the musty old rat smell.	讓門開著吧。也許有風吹進來，能把那股老鼠的霉味散一散。
Unfortunately, you don't speak the language of the little folk.	可惜你不會說這些嬌小族人的語言。
Don't even try it.  They're more agile than you are, and they outnumber you.	想都別想。他們比你敏捷得多，而且人數也比你多。
The Leprechaun King absolutely, positively forbids violence or weapons of any sort in his throne room.  With thoughts of the sling in your mind, you seem unable to turn those thoughts into movement.	地穴人國王絕對、明確禁止在他的王座廳內使用暴力或任何武器。儘管你心裡想著投石器，卻怎麼也無法把念頭化為行動。
The Leprechaun King's magic does not permit you to use weapons in the Throne Room.  Thus, while the sling is still in your pocket, you seem entirely unable to put it in your hand.	地穴人國王的魔法不允許你在王座廳內使用武器。因此，儘管投石器還放在你的口袋裡，你卻完全無法把它拿在手上。
Oh, no!  Now what are you going to do?	糟了！現在你該怎麼辦？
This looks like a bad situation.  Perhaps you should do something!	情況看起來不妙。也許你該做點什麼！
With a genuine four-leaf clover in your possession, the leprechauns fear and respect you.  Rather than risk offending you, they decide to leave you entirely alone.	你身上帶著一株真正的幸運草，地穴人們對你既畏懼又敬重。他們寧可完全不理你，也不願冒險冒犯你。
The guards catch you.  You spend the rest of your days peeling potatoes for the King of the Leprechauns.	衛兵抓住了你。你餘生都在替地穴人國王削馬鈴薯度過。
You can't play the fiddle while you're invisible.	你隱形的時候沒辦法演奏小提琴。
Wonderful job!  Leprechauns find fiddle music irresistible.  The moment they hear the music, they begin dancing a frenzied jig.	做得好極了！地穴人對小提琴的樂聲毫無抵抗力。他們一聽見音樂，立刻跳起狂熱的吉格舞。
Finally, swept away by the snappy music, the Leprechaun guards poof right out of the room.	最後，衛兵們被輕快的音樂沖昏了頭，一陣煙就從房間裡消失不見。
Carved into the top of this stone pillar is a huge four-leaf clover. Apparently the leprechauns who inhabit this underground sanctuary greatly fear and respect the power of the four-leaf clover!	這根石柱頂端雕刻著一株巨大的幸運草。看來居住在這處地底聖殿的地穴人，對幸運草的力量既畏懼又敬重！
Please don't move the carpet.  It hides the Dandelion Wine stains on the floor.	請不要移動這張地毯。它遮住了地上蒲公英酒的污漬。
What!?  And sit on the jewelled sceptre?!?	什麼！？坐在那根鑲滿珠寶的王杖上？！
You don't have time for that, Sir Graham.	格拉漢爵士，你沒時間做那件事。
Eating the mushroom can get you out of a tight spot, but not at the moment.	吃下蘑菇能讓你脫離險境，但現在還不是時候。
This luxurious carpet is the product of the Leprechaun's magical weaving talents.	這張華麗的地毯，是地穴人神奇織藝的產物。
The King of the Leprechauns is sitting on his stone throne, sceptre in hand.	地穴人國王坐在他的石座上，手裡握著王杖。
This is a rather simple stone throne, upon it sits the leprechaun kings jewelled sceptre.	這是一座相當樸素的石座，上面放著地穴人國王那根鑲滿珠寶的王杖。
This is a rather simple stone throne, compared to King Edward's.	比起愛德華國王的王座，這座石座顯得相當樸素。
There is no sceptre here.	這裡沒有王杖。
The sceptre is fashioned from gold and silver, and accented with emeralds.	這根王杖以金銀打造，並鑲嵌著翡翠點綴。
You can see a sceptre from where you are standing	從你站的位置可以看見一根王杖。
The shield is made of titanium and is rimmed with jewels.	靈盾以鈦金屬打造，邊緣鑲著珠寶。
You can see a shield from where you are standing.	從你站的位置可以看見靈盾。
This is the throne room of the Leprechaun King.	這裡是地穴人國王的王座廳。
The king has a sceptre.	國王手裡有一根王杖。
The king has a sceptre and there is a shield near the throne.	國王手裡有一根王杖，王座附近還有一面靈盾。
There is a sceptre on the throne.	王座上放著一根王杖。
There is a sceptre and shield near the throne.	王座附近有一根王杖和一面靈盾。
There is a shield near the throne.	王座附近有一面靈盾。
The leprechaun King is not here.	地穴人國王不在這裡。
By playing your fiddle,  the leprechaun King dances merrily away.	你演奏起小提琴，地穴人國王便歡快地跳著舞離開了。
The King of the Leprechauns is sitting on his throne.	地穴人國王坐在他的王座上。
Unfortunately, you do not speak the language of the little folk.	可惜你不會說這些嬌小族人的語言。
There are no Leprechauns here to talk to.	這裡沒有地穴人可以交談。
The Leprechaun King is not here.	地穴人國王不在這裡。
